# Circuit simulation architecture

**DO NOT INVENT RESULTS** — voltages, currents, and charge come from **AVR** or **SPICE** (see always-applied `no-invent-simulation.mdc`). UI may only mirror or lerp between those values.

Three layers — do not conflate them:

| Layer | Role | Key paths |
|-------|------|-----------|
| **Math engine** | DC voltages/currents | `circuit/dcSolver.ts`, `circuit/spice/client.ts`, `circuit/spice/worker.ts` (eecircuit-engine), `circuit/spice/pspiceCompat.ts`, `circuit/mnaLegacy.ts`, `circuit/spice/netlistExport.ts` |
| **Failure rules** | Blow detection, smoke, red X | `circuit/visuals.ts`, `CircuitSimState` / `ComponentSimFlags` in `circuit/solver.ts` |
| **Visuals** | Glow, wire dashes, heat | `ui/canvas/ComponentShape.tsx`, `circuit/currents.ts`, `index.css`, `simLiveStore` |

## Rules

- **No invented V/I/charge** — prefer ngspice node voltages and V-source branch currents; AVR for GPIO; never fake RC or rated-If overlays as if they were solved.
- **Blown parts are app logic**, not native ngspice. Export open circuits (~1 GΩ) in `netlistExport.ts` for both ngspice and legacy.
- Pass `resistorBlown` and `ledBlown` through cache keys, `refreshDcOperatingPoint`, and `solveDcCircuit`.
- On new blow: invalidate ngspice cache; sync re-solve via legacy for same-frame wire/heat update.
- Prefer ngspice branch currents for animations; legacy MNA is fallback when cache miss or worker unavailable.
- Do not change overload **animation timing or visuals** unless the user asks — fix circuit behavior separately.

## Verify

After sim changes: `npm run build`. For parser/worker changes, test with sim running and check solver badge + ngspice DC overlay.
